1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,150
Start with the intended
Custom Map and open Layers.

2
00:00:03,559 --> 00:00:08,930
For this exercise, prepare a separate
layer named G I S import, set Order to

3
00:00:08,930 --> 00:00:11,569
ten, and choose Data Layer as its Type.

4
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:15,970
Select the fictional floor-plan image
under Layer Image so the imported

5
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:17,819
shapes will have readable context.

6
00:00:18,190 --> 00:00:21,629
Select Add Layer and verify
the saved DataLayer row.

7
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:24,969
The earlier ground-floor layer
remains listed separately.

8
00:00:25,159 --> 00:00:28,800
Return to Custom Maps and choose
Import for the intended map.

9
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:32,089
Set Target Layer to
the G I S import layer.

10
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:37,790
The page lists GeoJSON, K M L and
K M Z as supported formats; this

11
00:00:37,790 --> 00:00:39,920
walkthrough uses GeoJSON only.

12
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:43,730
Use Choose File to select
the supplied fictional export

13
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:45,630
containing two named polygons.

14
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:50,320
Check the target and selected file
together, then select Import once.

15
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:53,460
Read Import History after
the upload finishes.

16
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:57,969
This recorded run has a GeoJSON
row with Complete status, a

17
00:00:57,969 --> 00:01:00,019
date and a blank Error column.

18
00:01:00,469 --> 00:01:05,750
The history uses the generic name
geojson-import dot json for this run.

19
00:01:06,209 --> 00:01:09,920
Completion confirms that processing
finished; the next step is to

20
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,730
inspect the actual regions.

21
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:16,260
The form above the history is ready for
another upload, so its current target

22
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:18,330
selection is a separate form value.

23
00:01:18,589 --> 00:01:22,240
Open Region Editor for the G
I S import layer, and wait for

24
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:23,770
the image and shapes to load.

25
00:01:24,369 --> 00:01:28,209
Both Training room, followed by
import, and Equipment, followed

26
00:01:28,209 --> 00:01:30,249
by import, appear in Regions.

27
00:01:30,740 --> 00:01:33,219
Their blue polygons sit
over the corresponding

28
00:01:33,219 --> 00:01:34,869
fictional spaces on the plan.

29
00:01:35,369 --> 00:01:38,969
Compare the names and boundaries with
the source file and intended layer.

30
00:01:39,369 --> 00:01:43,269
This visual check establishes more
than the Complete history entry alone.

31
00:01:43,559 --> 00:01:46,889
Select the training-room boundary
to open Region Properties.

32
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:49,699
Its imported Name and
Description are present.

33
00:01:50,039 --> 00:01:54,650
In this recorded example, the initial
Type is Custom, the Color is blue,

34
00:01:54,929 --> 00:01:58,249
and both Searchable in dispatch
and Dispatchable are checked.

35
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:02,440
Review these application settings
after an import rather than assuming

36
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:06,450
every property in an outside file
became the intended Resgrid setting.

37
00:02:06,909 --> 00:02:09,669
The form shows what this
region actually contains.

38
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:13,400
Change Type to Room and choose
the amber Color shown here.

39
00:02:13,839 --> 00:02:17,669
Clear Searchable in dispatch and
Dispatchable for this local review

40
00:02:17,669 --> 00:02:20,310
exercise, then select Save Region.

41
00:02:20,839 --> 00:02:22,730
Reopen the boundary after reload.

42
00:02:23,190 --> 00:02:26,540
The shape is amber, the
list says Room, and the form

43
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:28,510
retains both unchecked options.

44
00:02:28,770 --> 00:02:30,210
The original name remains.

45
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:33,710
This distinguishes the prepared
changes from the saved region

46
00:02:33,739 --> 00:02:35,589
that the application now returns.

47
00:02:35,739 --> 00:02:37,469
Repeat the review for Equipment.

48
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:41,359
Set its Type to Room and clear
both availability options,

49
00:02:41,669 --> 00:02:43,339
then select Save Region.

50
00:02:43,770 --> 00:02:45,869
Reload and select that boundary again.

51
00:02:46,270 --> 00:02:50,709
Its name, Room type, blue Color
and unchecked options are retained.

52
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:54,479
Both imported regions are
still listed, and neither has a

53
00:02:54,479 --> 00:02:56,479
Dispatchable badge in this final view.

54
00:02:56,880 --> 00:03:00,550
Reviewing one imported shape does
not replace checking the others.

55
00:03:00,699 --> 00:03:02,350
Return to Import History.

56
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:06,730
The original completed run remains
available after the region edits.

57
00:03:07,170 --> 00:03:10,379
The new-upload form now shows
the ground-floor layer, which

58
00:03:10,379 --> 00:03:12,079
is the first choice in its list.

59
00:03:12,499 --> 00:03:16,039
For a subsequent file, deliberately
select the intended Target

60
00:03:16,039 --> 00:03:17,769
Layer again before importing.

61
00:03:18,219 --> 00:03:21,549
Use the history to review the
completed run and the form to

62
00:03:21,549 --> 00:03:25,140
prepare the next operation; they
show different parts of the workflow.

63
00:03:25,389 --> 00:03:29,760
This process can help security companies,
search-and-rescue teams, wildland

64
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:34,990
contractors and industrial emergency teams
bring permitted site areas into Resgrid.

65
00:03:35,429 --> 00:03:39,469
Community paramedicine, mental
health response, fire and E M S

66
00:03:39,469 --> 00:03:43,589
departments can use the same checks
for appropriate coordination locations.

67
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:49,269
Choose the correct file and target layer,
inspect the imported geometry, review each

68
00:03:49,269 --> 00:03:54,329
region’s application settings, save, and
reopen the result before relying on it.


